Automatic note creation uses the bounded commit classifier to acknowledge a nonempty metadata-only commit without creating a notes association; commits touching source remain material, and empty commits retain existing note-writer behavior. Metadata includes .span, .spans and the configured span root. Merge-parent paths and rename source/destination paths participate in classification, so moving metadata into source remains material; classifier failures retain receipts for retry. Card main-432 removes the former Claude Stop consumer while preserving this writer policy. The receipt regression tests exercise metadata-only exclusion for Claude and Codex; they do not establish the configured-root or mixed-commit cases formerly checked through Stop.
